cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived tables, please cite it as below, together with the companion paper."
type: software
title: "Ukraine strikes × hromada resilience: analysis pipeline"
version: "1.1-step2"
license:
  - MIT
  - ODbL-1.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ubeccommon/ubec_ukraine_resilience"
authors:
  - family-names: Garand
    given-names: Michel
    affiliation: "UBEC Platform"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python and QGIS pipeline linking Russian strikes and
  air-raid alerts in Ukraine to hromada-level fiscal capacity, local
  budgets, displacement context and monthly night-light trajectories,
  2022–2026. Code is MIT; small derived tables are ODbL 1.0;
  documentation and figures are CC BY 4.0. Raw data and data whose
  terms forbid redistribution are not included.
keywords:
  - Ukraine
  - hromada
  - war
  - air-raid alerts
  - night lights
  - local government finance
  - resilience
  - spatial analysis
  - QGIS
preferred-citation:
